KO: "모두 불태워버리자!"
ZH: "\n炸了他們。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf01Subtitle
US: "*Welcome back, General"
DE: "*Welcome back, General"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nBienvenido, general."
IT: "*Welcome back, General"
KO: "안녕하셨습니까, 장군님"
ZH: "\n歡迎歸隊，將軍。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf02Subtitle
US: "*The GLA launched their missile from the Baikonur Facility early this morning. Intel reports that they are preparing a second launch"
DE: "*The GLA launched their missile from the Baikonur Facility early this morning. Intel reports that they are preparing a second launch"
FR: "***"
ES: "***"
IT: "\nL'ELG ha lanciato il suo missile dal poligono di Baikonur stamattina all'alba.\nPare che stiano preparando un secondo lancio."
KO: "\n오늘 오전 GLA는 바이코누르 발사 시설에서 미사일을 발사했습니다.\n정보에 따르면 그들은 두번째 발사를 준비한다고 합니다."
ZH: "\n今天稍早全球解放軍在巴以庫爾太空城進行飛彈發射，情報指出他們正在準備發射第二枚飛彈的相關事\n宜。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf03Subtitle
US: "*Use of this missile will severely weaken our foothold in Europe. It is vital that we remove this threat"
DE: "*Use of this missile will severely weaken our foothold in Europe. It is vital that we remove this threat"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nEste misil debilitará muchísimo nuestra posición en Europa.\nEs vital eliminar esta amenaza."
IT: "\nL'uso del missile indebolirà pesantemente la nostra influenza in Europa:\ndovete eliminare questa minaccia."
KO: "\n이 미사일이 발사되면 유럽에서 우리의 입지가 매우 약해질 것입니다.\n이 위협을 제거하는 것이 매우 중요합니다."
ZH: "\n飛彈的發射將嚴重的削弱我方在歐洲據點的勢力，因此如何解除這個威脅當是刻不容緩的事。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf04Subtitle
US: "*Our sources indicate that the next missile is being transported to the launch facility by train. These tracks are the only way into the facility"
DE: "*Our sources indicate that the next missile is being transported to the launch facility by train. These tracks are the only way into the facility"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nEl próximo misil se llevará en tren a la planta de lanzamiento.\n\nEstas vías son el único acceso a la planta."
IT: "\nLe nostre fonti indicano che il prossimo missile è trasportato da un treno:\nquesti binari sono l'unico accesso alla struttura."
KO: "\n다음 미사일은 열차를 통해 발사 시설로 운반중이라는 정보가 들어왔습니다.\n이 철로는 발사 시설로 통하는 유일한 길입니다."
ZH: "\n有消息來源指出下一枚飛彈將利用火車運送至發射中心，而這些鐵軌將是通往目的地的唯一途徑。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf05Subtitle
US: "*If we can intercept that train in time, we can use it as cover to infiltrate the base"
DE: "*If we can intercept that train in time, we can use it as cover to infiltrate the base"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nSi interceptamos el tren a tiempo, podremos usarlo para entrar en la base."
IT: "\nSe riuscirete a intercettare il treno in tempo, lo useremo\ncome copertura per infiltrarci nella base."
KO: "시간에 맞게 기차를 탈취한다면 우리는 들키지 않고 기지로 침투할 수 있을 것입니다."
ZH: "\n如果可以及時攔截那輛火車，將可利用它掩護我們滲透到基地內部。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf06Subtitle
US: "*The first step in completing our mission is to secure and hold this Train Depot"
DE: "*The first step in completing our mission is to secure and hold this Train Depot"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nEl primer paso de nuestra misión es asegurar y controlar este tren."
IT: "\nCome prima cosa dovete conquistare e presidiare questo deposito ferroviario."
KO: "임무 수행을 위한 첫번째 단계는 이 기차역을 확보하고 방어하는 것입니다."
ZH: "\n想要完成任務的第一步，就是安全佔領火車站。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

DIALOGEVENT:MisUSA01xBrf07Subtitle
US: "*Good luck, General"
DE: "*Good luck, General"
FR: "***"
ES: "\nBuena suerte, general."
IT: "\nBuona fortuna, generale."
KO: "행운을 빕니다, 장군님."
ZH: "\n祝你好運，將軍。"
BP: "***"
PL: "***"
END

